From: w478 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/lima: start a deferred task before the one after it

478-0106 lets drm_sched hand lima a second task while one runs (credit
limit 2). When the IRQ handler cannot start the parked task itself (its
page directory is not loaded, or lima.irq_start=N), it queues start_work
and signals the finished task at once, which frees a credit: drm_sched can
then call run_job for the task after the parked one before start_work has
run, find the pipe idle and start it first. Two tasks of one pipe then ran
out of order, and the Demo's frozen pictures were wrong in three of six
scenes with irq_start=N (boot 478-3: irq_start=N alone gave the wrong
bytes, every other switch alone the right ones).

In run_job, start the parked task first and park the new one behind it.
The IRQ handler's own path and start_work are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
@@ -406,7 +406,22 @@
 		pipe->task_prepare(pipe, task);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&pipe->hw_lock, flags);
-	if (!pipe->current_task) {
+	if (!pipe->current_task && pipe->next_task) {
+		/*
+		 * The IRQ handler deferred the parked task to start_work
+		 * (its page directory was not loaded, or irq_start=N) and
+		 * signalled the finished one, so drm_sched may hand us the
+		 * task after it before start_work has run. The parked one
+		 * goes first: starting this one now would run two tasks of
+		 * the pipe out of order (the Demo's frozen pictures were
+		 * wrong in three of six scenes with irq_start=N, boot 478-3).
+		 * start_work finds the pipe busy and does nothing.
+		 */
+		struct lima_sched_task *first = pipe->next_task;
+
+		pipe->next_task = task;
+		old = lima_sched_hw_start(pipe, first);
+	} else if (!pipe->current_task) {
 		old = lima_sched_hw_start(pipe, task);
 	} else {
 		/* the IRQ handler of the running task will start it */
